# Launch Rules

## Security

- Stripe webhook handlers MUST verify the signature on every incoming event.
- `next.config.js` must NOT have `ignoreBuildErrors: true` or
  `ignoreDuringBuilds: true` in production builds.
- No secrets in code. Use environment variables only.
- PCI-DSS scope: card data must never touch EUshop servers. Use Stripe Elements
  or Stripe Checkout only. Verify this holds after any Connect changes.

## Testing requirements (Phase 4.3)

Compliance engine tests are the highest priority. Required fixture tests:
- DAC7: exactly 30 transactions (excluded), 31 (reportable)
- DAC7: exactly €2,000 consideration (excluded), €2,001 (reportable)
- VAT: known rate per destination country (DE=7%, IE=0%, DK=25%)
- Allergen filter: item with allergen excluded when filter active

## SEO (Phase 4.1)

- JSON-LD structured data must NOT repeat unverified compliance claims.
- Use Next.js Metadata API (or `next/head` for Pages Router) consistently.
- `hreflang` tags required for language/locale variants.
- Canonical URLs required for currency/locale variants of the same product.
